## Booting the emulator (do this first; it has sharp edges)

The AVD is `Medium_Phone_API_36` (API 36, arm64, Play Store image). A naive
`emulator -avd ... &` from an agent shell does **not** work reliably — use the
committed launcher:

```bash
python3 MDRTAcademy/scripts/agent-boot-emulator.py        # detaches + cold-boots
export PATH="$HOME/Library/Android/sdk/platform-tools:$PATH"
adb wait-for-device
until [ "$(adb shell getprop sys.boot_completed | tr -d '\r')" = "1" ]; do sleep 2; done
```

A clean cold boot is ~15-20s. The launcher exists because two failure modes
bite a plain background launch (both documented in the script header):

1. **Process-group teardown.** When you background the emulator and the
   spawning agent shell returns, the harness tears down the process group and
   the emulator dies a second or two later ("boots, then the window vanishes").
   macOS has no `setsid`, so the launcher daemonizes with a double-fork +
   `os.setsid()` to fully detach. `nohup`/`disown` alone is **not** enough.
2. **Corrupt Quick Boot snapshot.** A stale `default_boot` snapshot can fail
   GPU restore (`ERROR | Failed to find ColorBuffer:0`) and crash qemu right
   after the window appears. The launcher always passes `-no-snapshot-load`,
   and the AVD's `config.ini` is set to `fastboot.forceColdBoot = yes` so even
   a plain launch is safe. If you ever see the ColorBuffer crash again, delete
   `~/.android/avd/Medium_Phone.avd/snapshots/default_boot` (the AVD's data
   dir is `Medium_Phone.avd`, not `Medium_Phone_API_36.avd`).

The launcher also uses software GPU (`-gpu swiftshader_indirect`) for headless
reliability and `-partition-size 8192` so large (~128 MB) APK installs don't
hit `INSTALL_FAILED_INSUFFICIENT_STORAGE`. If `/data` still fills up, `adb
uninstall com.mdrt.mdrtacademy.qa` before reinstalling reclaims the most space.
To shut the emulator down cleanly: `adb emu kill`.

## On-device interaction (the agent's "browser" for mobile)
- Install / update an APK: `adb install -r path/to/app-qa-debug.apk`
- Force-stop to reset state: `adb shell am force-stop com.mdrt.mdrtacademy.qa`
- Launch: `adb shell monkey -p com.mdrt.mdrtacademy.qa -c android.intent.category.LAUNCHER 1`
- Identify topmost Activity: `adb shell dumpsys activity activities | grep topResumedActivity`
- Tap / swipe: `adb shell input tap <x> <y>` / `adb shell input swipe <x1> <y1> <x2> <y2> <duration_ms>`
- Get device resolution (for scaling taps): `adb shell wm size`
- Screenshot (3-step idiom — capture, pull, clean up):
  ```bash
  adb shell screencap -p /sdcard/s.png \
    && adb pull /sdcard/s.png /tmp/<name>.png \
    && adb shell rm /sdcard/s.png
  ```
- Force 3-button nav (matches the most-reported bug scenario):
  ```bash
  adb shell cmd overlay enable com.android.internal.systemui.navbar.threebutton
  adb shell cmd overlay disable com.android.internal.systemui.navbar.gestural
  ```
- Restore gesture nav: swap the two `enable`/`disable` overlay names.

After taking a screenshot, **read it back into the chat as an artifact** so the user can see what the device actually rendered.

## User Context
- The primary developer is a **Ruby on Rails / web backend developer** with minimal Android / Kotlin experience
- Explain Android / Kotlin / Gradle concepts using Rails / web analogies when helpful
- Be explicit about where files go and why — don't assume familiarity with Android project conventions
- When explaining Android patterns, relate to MVC (which Rails devs know well):
  - `Activity` / `Fragment` = Rails Controller (with View merged in for screen-level UI)
  - Layout XML (`res/layout/*.xml`) = ERB / HTML view template (declarative, mostly inert)
  - `ViewModel` (AAC) = service object / presenter — survives config changes the way a server-side controller survives a single request
  - Data class / `data class Foo(...)` in `model/` = ActiveRecord model **without** DB persistence (no rows, just shape)
  - `NetworkingService` (Retrofit) = HTTP client / API wrapper (like Faraday / HTTParty wrappers)
  - `SharedPreferences` = session / cookies (small key-value, on-disk, app-scoped)
  - Room database = ActiveRecord with SQLite (DAOs ≈ scopes, `@Entity` ≈ a model class)
  - `LiveData` / `Flow` / EventBus = pub/sub / `ActiveSupport::Notifications`
  - `Intent` = a serialized route + params (you "navigate" by handing the OS an `Intent` the way you'd `redirect_to`)
  - Gradle = Bundler + Rake + Webpacker in one. `build.gradle` is `Gemfile` + `Rakefile` + asset pipeline config.
  - AndroidManifest.xml = `config/routes.rb` + `config/application.rb` + permissions declarations, fused into one XML file
  - `R.string.foo` lookups in code = `t('foo')` i18n lookups in Rails views

## Common gotchas (recognize these failure modes)
- **JAVA_HOME / ANDROID_HOME / PATH symptoms** → see the "Required environment" section above. This is the #1 cause of confusing Gradle / adb failures in this repo and the symptoms are non-obvious; check that section first before chasing anything else.
- **`Could not resolve all artifacts`** (NOT paired with a "compatible with Java 8" variant message) → genuine network issue or proxy. Retry; if it persists, check `gradle.properties` for `org.gradle.jvmargs` and proxy settings. (If you DO see the Java 8 variant message, it's `JAVA_HOME`, not the network.)
- **App installs but crashes on launch with `INSTALL_FAILED_UPDATE_INCOMPATIBLE`** → the signing certificate changed (you built a release variant over a debug, or vice versa). `adb uninstall <package_id>` then re-install.
- **`adb` reports `device offline`** → `adb kill-server && adb start-server && adb devices`. If still offline, the emulator process is wedged; kill and reboot it.
- **Emulator "boots for a second then closes"** → almost always one of the two boot failure modes in the "Booting the emulator" section: a corrupt Quick Boot snapshot (`Failed to find ColorBuffer:0` in the log) or process-group teardown of a backgrounded launch. Use `MDRTAcademy/scripts/agent-boot-emulator.py` rather than launching `emulator` directly.
- **`INSTALL_FAILED_INSUFFICIENT_STORAGE` on a ~128 MB APK** → the AVD `/data` partition is near full. `adb uninstall com.mdrt.mdrtacademy.qa` first, and/or relaunch via the script (it passes `-partition-size 8192`).
- **Edge-to-edge layout regression on Android 15 / SDK 35+** → `BaseActivity.kt` has the inset listener and bleed-color hooks; check `shouldApplyDefaultSystemBarInsets()`, `statusBarBleedColor()`, `navigationBarBleedColor()`, and `onSystemBarInsetsChanged()` before adding ad-hoc per-Activity insets handling. See `docs/agentic-showcase-edge-to-edge-deepdive.md` for the full rationale.
